  <section class="section center" style="padding-top: clamp(120px, 14vw, 180px);">
    <div class="wrap reveal">
      <h2 class="h1" style="max-width: 18ch; margin: 0 auto;">Beautiful enough to open. <span class="grad-text">Clever enough that you rarely need to.</span></h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="features" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="wrap">

      <div class="feature">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Journeys</span>
          <h2 class="h2">A map of everywhere you're going.</h2>
          <p class="lede">Every upcoming journey drawn across Britain, with your train moving along its route. The one under way gets the spotlight; everything after is a simple countdown.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-media reveal d1"><div class="phone"><img src="/assets/img/enroute/home-dark.png" alt="Journeys home in dark mode" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature flip">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Your train</span>
          <h2 class="h2">Everything about your train. Honestly.</h2>
          <p class="lede">Delays shown with the timetable struck through. Every stop on the route. And a platform that never pretends to be more certain than it is.</p>
          <div class="platform-pills">
            <div class="pill confirmed">Platform<b>3</b><span>Confirmed</span></div>
            <div class="pill expected">Platform<b>3</b><span>Expected</span></div>
            <div class="pill notyet">Platform<b>–</b><span>Not yet</span></div>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>See where your inbound train is before it reaches you</li>
            <li>Position between stations is shown as an estimate, never as GPS</li>
            <li>Every screen tells you how fresh the information is</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-media reveal d1"><div class="phone"><img src="/assets/img/enroute/calling-points.png" alt="Calling-point timeline" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Lock Screen &amp; Dynamic Island</span>
          <h2 class="h2">Your journey, without opening the app.</h2>
          <p class="lede">A Live Activity follows your train: platform, expected times, delay and progress. Notifications arrive for the moments that matter, once each.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Platform confirmed</li>
            <li>Your train is in</li>
            <li>Arriving at your stop</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-media reveal d1"><div class="phone"><img src="/assets/img/enroute/live-activity.png" alt="Live Activity on the Lock Screen" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature flip">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Departures</span>
          <h2 class="h2">The board for the station you're standing in.</h2>
          <p class="lede">One tap shows departures from your nearest station. Track any train in three taps. Your location is used once, to find the station, and never stored.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-media reveal d1"><div class="phone"><img src="/assets/img/enroute/departure-board.png" alt="Departure board for the nearest station" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div></div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section er-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Friends</span>
          <h2 class="h2">Know when to leave for the station.</h2>
          <p class="lede">Share your train with whoever's picking you up. They see the route, the train's estimated position and when it's due in. They never see you.</p>
          <ul style="color:#d9e6e4;">
            <li>Share every journey, or choose each one</li>
            <li>Hide any trip with one switch. Perfect for a surprise visit</li>
            <li>Invite by iMessage; remove access at any moment</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-media reveal d1"><div class="phone"><img src="/assets/img/enroute/friends.png" alt="A friend's view of a shared journey" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Passport</span>
          <h2 class="h2">Every journey, kept for good.</h2>
          <p class="lede">When a trip ends, Enroute keeps a permanent record: timetable and actual times side by side, the route and the platforms. Your history never depends on a railway server.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Statistics that only count what was really recorded</li>
            <li>Delay Repay guidance when you arrive 15+ minutes late</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-media reveal d1"><div class="phone"><img src="/assets/img/enroute/passport.png" alt="Passport statistics" width="460" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tight" style="background: var(--bg-alt);">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="center reveal" style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
        <span class="eyebrow">Yours, and private</span>
        <h2 class="h2">We don't keep a database of anyone's travel.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid three">
        <div class="card reveal"><h3 class="h3">No account needed</h3><p>Track trains straight away. Enroute never asks for your email address.</p></div>
        <div class="card reveal d1"><h3 class="h3">Your own iCloud</h3><p>Journeys sync through your private iCloud, not our servers.</p></div>
        <div class="card reveal d2"><h3 class="h3">Works offline</h3><p>Your journeys are on your iPhone, with or without signal.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

